The United States Government has been in direct communication with the Government of the Republic of Haiti since July 2010. Through this direct communication, and in coordination with the Haitian Government, the United States has provided humanitarian assistance, support for law and order, and humanitarian and development assistance. This includes:

1.  Over $300 million in direct humanitarian assistance, including $24.4 million in cash assistance and $275,000 in food, shelter, medical, and other needs-based assistance, delivered via the UNHCR;

2.  $14 million in direct humanitarian assistance to assist with the needs of Haitian refugees in the United States and Canada;

3.  $50 million in humanitarian assistance, including $34 million in food and $16 million in shelter, to the Haitian government;

